abstract: 'Software for the planar laser-induced fluorescence acquisition apparatus used in Arij Asad''s
  PhD research, Mixing behaviour of plumes, at the University of Bristol. The package contains a Teledyne
  DALSA camera receiver, SDK build helper, network frame-storage request tool, retained BeagleBone controller
  and simulated-SDK checks.


  The receiver acquires continuously and stores the latest complete frame on request. Supporting files
  document the acquisition sequence, interface circuits and apparatus assembly, with installation instructions
  and the archived network protocol. The source preserves GitHub release thesis-code-2026-09-27.


  The receiver targets Linux with an externally installed GigE-V SDK. Vendor libraries and examples are
  not included. The BeagleBone program records the original apparatus configuration; its known GPIO issues
  are described in the guide. Simulated receiver checks are distinct from camera and laser operation.


  Source code is licensed under MIT; thesis figures and documentation are licensed under CC BY 4.0.'
